# Simple, human writing (law)

Read skill **forja-simple-writing** when drafting long prose or when writing feels padded.

Write like a sharp teammate. Short sentences. One claim each. Lead with the answer. Say it once, then stop.

| Ban | |
|-----|--|
| Contrarian / twist openers | “everyone thinks X, but…” / “the real issue is…” |
| Stacked anaphora / “Not X — Y” cadence | |
| Hedge fog | “should work”, “mostly fixed”, “it’s worth noting” |
| Empty scaffolding | “Here’s how…”, “Let’s dive in”, “Key takeaways” |
| Bold/emoji theater, synonym churn, false balance, corporate calm | |
| List inflation / coverage padding | |

**Sniff:** delete the first sentence and every “Not X — Y” line. If nothing is lost, rewrite.

Shape: answer first · evidence when stating facts · tables/code over prose · casual with this user.
